CORE
main.c
--unwind 1 --rounds 2 --por --datarace
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
Control for `atomic_section_const_index_framing`: same constant-resolved
index inside an atomic section (both threads call `bump(0)`), but `main`
also writes `arr[0]` directly, unprotected, after creating both threads and
before joining them -- a genuine race on the exact element the fix's
guard-skip path treats as "never touched" by the symbolic-index load. Must
stay FAILED before and after this fix: proves the fix (falling back to the
plain unconditioned rename when the renamed index is a constant) does not
suppress a real race in this same code path, only the vacuous-generation
framing bug on the genuinely-untouched element.
